# ─── Secrets and local environment ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The single most important block in this file, and the only one with a gate
# behind it: `make check` runs `make secrets` (gitleaks) so this is enforced,
# not merely requested. A .gitignore alone has never stopped a `git add -f`.
#
# UsArr's config carries *Arr API keys (full admin on those instances), media
# server tokens, and the master encryption key that opens all of them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
.envrc
secrets/
secret.key
secret.key.new
keys/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
# Test fixtures may legitimately carry throwaway key material.
!**/testdata/**/*.pem
!**/testdata/**/*.key

# ─── Build artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/usarr
/usarr.exe
/usarr-*
dist/
build/
bin/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
!**/testdata/**/*.out
cover.out
cover.html
coverage.*
*.prof
*.pprof

# ─── Go ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
vendor/
go.work
go.work.sum

# ─── Frontend (SvelteKit / Vite / pnpm) ──────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
web/build/
web/.svelte-kit/
web/.vite/
web/dist/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-debug.log*
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─── SQLite ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WAL mode produces -wal and -shm alongside every database. All three are
# runtime state; never commit any of them, and never back up the .db alone while
# running (use `VACUUM INTO` — docs/CONFIGURATION.md §6).
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
usarr.db*
cache.db*

# ─── Runtime data directories ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local bind mounts and dev state. `/config` holds keys/, providers/, backups/
# and the database; `/data` holds the caches and logs. Neither ever goes in git.
/config/
/data/
/.dev/
/logs/
/backups/
/tmp/

# ─── Local compose stacks and their seeded state ─────────────────────────────
# NOTHING under deploy/compose/ that contains an *Arr config volume is
# committed — not even "intentionally fake" seed directories. A generated 32-hex
# API key is indistinguishable from a real one to a reviewer and to a secret
# scanner, so the first person to regenerate a seed from a working stack commits
# a live credential. The reproducible path is `make seed`, a script that drives
# each app's own API with fixed, obviously-fake constants at run time.
# See docs/DEVELOPMENT.md §7.1.
deploy/compose/**/config/
deploy/compose/**/appdata/
deploy/compose/seed/

# go-vcr cassettes ARE committed (scrubbed by a recorder hook), but unscrubbed
# in-progress recordings are not.
testdata/cassettes/*.unscrubbed.yaml
testdata/cassettes/**/*.raw.yaml

# ─── Editors and IDEs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.\#*
\#*\#
.projectile
nvim.log
.zed/

# ─── OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─── Misc ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.bak
*.tmp
*.orig
*.rej
.cache/
.direnv/
.tool-versions.local
